cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this measurement or this code, cite it as below."
title: "Multiplicative correlations in the Goldbach error field: an empirical study"
abstract: >-
  A smooth weighted balanced Goldbach count defines an error field eps(N). Its two-point
  correlation across multiplicative dilations, c(k) = corr(eps(N), eps(kN)), is negative at
  prime ratios and near zero at composite ratios, a sign pattern (-1)^omega(k) that holds from
  N = 1.2e4 to 1e9. No mechanism is proposed; the paper records the measurement, the checks it
  survives, and the explanations it excludes.
authors:
